<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10993" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conversātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		converso (not ante-Aug.). * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Frequent use</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ben. 3, 2, 2</span></i>; cf. Cod. Th. 11, 21, 1
			al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Frequent abode in a place</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 10,
				33, 51, § 100</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 11, 7, 12, §
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Intercourse, conversation</i> (so most freq.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">licentiosior cum viris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Exc. Contr. 6, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 102, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 7, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 3, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12,
				49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Or. 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter servos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					1, 2, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
